I’m sorry, but I don’t have the ability to make live calls to external services such as VirusTotal.  
If you’d like to retrieve the sibling domains for **amazon.com** yourself, you can use the following cURL command (replace `magic_key001` with your actual API key if it differs):

```bash
curl -X GET "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/amazon.com/sibling-domains?cursor=next123" \
     -H "x-apikey: magic_key001"
```

A typical JSON response will look something like this:

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "example1.com",
      "type": "domains",
      "attributes": {
        "last_analysis_stats": {
          "harmless": 10,
          "malicious": 0,
          "suspicious": 0,
          "undetected": 5,
          "timeout": 0
        },
        "last_analysis_date": 1712345678,
        "last_analysis_results": { /* ... */ }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "example2.net",
      "type": "domains",
      "attributes": {
        "last_analysis_stats": {
          "harmless": 8,
          "malicious": 1,
          "suspicious": 0,
          "undetected": 6,
          "timeout": 0
        },
        "last_analysis_date": 1712345679,
        "last_analysis_results": { /* ... */ }
      }
    }
    /* more sibling domains */
  ],
  "meta": {
    "cursor": "next123",
    "total": 42
  }
}
```

If you run the command above, you’ll receive the actual list of sibling domains along with their analysis statistics. Let me know if you need help interpreting the response or automating the request!
